WEBVTT

00:00:57.756 --> 00:01:00.316
But the problem is ...

00:01:00.316 --> 00:01:01.676
we’ve left it too late.

00:01:03.716 --> 00:01:06.756
We can't now do it fast enough.

00:01:07.956 --> 00:01:11.036
I've been working on climate change
for more than 20 years,

00:01:11.036 --> 00:01:13.516
and I’ve talked about it
in boardrooms and classrooms

00:01:13.516 --> 00:01:15.196
and everywhere in between,

00:01:15.196 --> 00:01:18.196
and I was shocked when I found this out,

00:01:18.196 --> 00:01:20.956
but the science is utterly ...

00:01:20.956 --> 00:01:21.956
utterly clear.

00:01:23.156 --> 00:01:26.436
If we’re going to have a fighting chance
of staying below 1.5 degrees,

00:01:26.436 --> 00:01:28.596
that “safe limit,”

00:01:28.596 --> 00:01:31.716
we have to have carbon removals,